  "notes": "A row of dominoes set up and knocked over, stereo, 'from one side to the other' (author), Sony ECM-99 stereo mic to a MiniDisc recorder. The spectrogram shows DENSE clatter filling 0.10-1.40 s (the row falling, hits overlapping so the onset counter only finds 10) and three separate late tiles at about 1.5, 1.6 and 1.8 s, then silence: exactly a 1.5 s fall that thins out. Natural left-to-right spread = the row-by-row fall; floor -79.5 dBFS (cleanest of the cascade set), peak -6.8 dBFS, rolloff95 10.0 kHz, narrow ring at 8.5-10 kHz. Dominoes on a table top: slightly woody, not glazed ceramic: pitch up +1..+2 st if it reads dull. For 3,000-tile density layer two copies 0.15-0.25 s apart with +-0.4 st. CC BY 4.0 (FreqMan): needs credit.",
